    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nThere is an example that imitates the word textobject with optional trailing whitespace:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\r\n\t\tw = { \"()()%f[%w]%w+()[ \\t]*()\" },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works well, but I want to achieve the opposite behavior: imitate the word textobject with optional leading whitespace. However, this does not work:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\r\n\t\tw = { \"()[ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is very close to the behavior I want:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\r\n\t\tw = { \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut it does not work correctly at the first word, i.e.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfor text:\r\n**the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog**\r\n\r\nnow:\r\n**the( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\r\n\r\ni want:\r\n**(the)( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs this possible?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is an example that imitates the word textobject with optional trailing whitespace:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { &quot;()()%f[%w]%w+()[ \\t]*()&quot; },\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>()()%f[%w]%w+()[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This works well, but I want to achieve the opposite behavior: imitate the word textobject with optional leading whitespace. However, this does not work:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { &quot;()[ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()&quot; },\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>()[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()%f[%w]%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is very close to the behavior I want:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { &quot;()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()&quot; },\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>()%f[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>][ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()%f[%w]%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">but it does not work correctly at the first word, i.e.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"for text:\n**the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog**\n\nnow:\n**the( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\n\ni want:\n**(the)( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">for text:\n**the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog**\n\nnow:\n**the( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\n\ni want:\n**(the)( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this possible?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nThere is an example that imitates the word textobject with optional trailing whitespace:\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { \"()()%f[%w]%w+()[ \\t]*()\" },\n\t},\n})\nThis works well, but I want to achieve the opposite behavior: imitate the word textobject with optional leading whitespace. However, this does not work:\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { \"()[ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" },\n\t},\n})\nThis is very close to the behavior I want:\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" },\n\t},\n})\nbut it does not work correctly at the first word, i.e.\nfor text:\n**the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog**\n\nnow:\n**the( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\n\ni want:\n**(the)( quick)( brown)( fox)( jumps)( over)( the)( lazy)( dog)**\n\nIs this possible?",
