                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "Thanks for the reply\r\nHowever, this cannot select the first `the` because there is an asterisk before it, it is not at the start of the line.\r\n\r\nI previously thought about using a composed pattern, like this:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\r\n\t\tw = { { \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\", \"%f[%w]%w+\" } },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nor\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\r\n\t\tw = { { \"%f[%w]%w+\", \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" } },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe result is that their order doesn’t matter; as you said, the pattern with the smallest width wins.\r\n",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the reply<br>\nHowever, this cannot select the first <code class=\"notranslate\">the</code> because there is an asterisk before it, it is not at the start of the line.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I previously thought about using a composed pattern, like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { { &quot;()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()&quot;, &quot;%f[%w]%w+&quot; } },\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>()%f[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>][ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()%f[%w]%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>%f[%w]%w+<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>} },\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">or</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { { &quot;%f[%w]%w+&quot;, &quot;()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()&quot; } },\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>%f[%w]%w+<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>()%f[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>][ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()%f[%w]%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>} },\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The result is that their order doesn’t matter; as you said, the pattern with the smallest width wins.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Thanks for the reply\nHowever, this cannot select the first the because there is an asterisk before it, it is not at the start of the line.\nI previously thought about using a composed pattern, like this:\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { { \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\", \"%f[%w]%w+\" } },\n\t},\n})\nor\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n\tcustom_textobjects = {\n\t\tw = { { \"%f[%w]%w+\", \"()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()\" } },\n\t},\n})\nThe result is that their order doesn’t matter; as you said, the pattern with the smallest width wins.",
