                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Ah, sorry, I misunderstood the meaning of `**`. Didn't realize that they were part of the text.\r\n\r\nI am afraid, in this case it is either add patterns on a case-by-case basis or pivot from using Lua patterns in favor of custom function. My suggestion would be the first one, but the following one makes it work for the original case (but there are still cases for which it won't work and even through an error):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    w = {\r\n      {\r\n        '^()%w+()',\r\n        '^[^ \\t%w]+()()%w+()()',\r\n        '()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()',\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Ah, sorry, I misunderstood the meaning of <code class=\"notranslate\">**</code>. Didn't realize that they were part of the text.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, in this case it is either add patterns on a case-by-case basis or pivot from using Lua patterns in favor of custom function. My suggestion would be the first one, but the following one makes it work for the original case (but there are still cases for which it won't work and even through an error):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    w = {\n      {\n        '^()%w+()',\n        '^[^ \\t%w]+()()%w+()()',\n        '()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()',\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      {\n        <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^()%w+()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n        <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^[^ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>%w]+()()%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n        <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>()%f[ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>][ <span class=\"pl-cce\">\\t</span>]*()%f[%w]%w+()()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Ah, sorry, I misunderstood the meaning of **. Didn't realize that they were part of the text.\nI am afraid, in this case it is either add patterns on a case-by-case basis or pivot from using Lua patterns in favor of custom function. My suggestion would be the first one, but the following one makes it work for the original case (but there are still cases for which it won't work and even through an error):\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    w = {\n      {\n        '^()%w+()',\n        '^[^ \\t%w]+()()%w+()()',\n        '()%f[ \\t][ \\t]*()%f[%w]%w+()()',\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})",
